# Mintlify automatically ignores these files and directories:
# .git, .github, .claude, .agents, .idea, node_modules,
# README.md, LICENSE.md, CHANGELOG.md, CONTRIBUTING.md

# Draft content
drafts/
*.draft.mdx

# Example sources & downloadable data — 138 MB that Mintlify walks but never
# serves.  Two mechanisms put this content on the site, and neither needs the
# file present at serve time:
#
#   1. Inlined at conversion.  literalinclude resolves against the HUGO tree
#      (docs/content/examples/), embedding the text straight into the MDX —
#      1941 {/* Source: /examples/... */} blocks from 326 source files.
#   2. Linked to GitHub.  Downloads point at raw.githubusercontent.com, not at
#      this site (118 raw URLs + 9 blob links; zero local path references).
#
# So this directory is a GIT PAYLOAD, not site content: it must stay COMMITTED
# so those raw.githubusercontent.com URLs resolve, but Mintlify has no reason to
# traverse it.  Ignoring it took the walked tree from 297 MB to ~159 MB after
# `npx mint dev` OOM'd against Node's 2 GB default heap.
#
# Tripwire: if a page ever switches from a GitHub URL to a relative link into
# examples/, this ignore would silently 404 it.  Link to GitHub, or revisit this.
content/examples/
